{"availability":"available","full":"exsitu-projects/lorgnette","name":"lorgnette","description":"👓 Lorgnette is a framework to create code editors with malleable projections of pieces of code.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":22,"forks":3,"created":"2023-07-27T11:45:34Z","updated":"2024-05-13T00:14:44Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"","topics":["code-editor","projection"],"demo":"https://exsitu-projects.github.io/lorgnette/playground/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T13:20:05.074Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T13:20:05.074Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T13:20:05.074Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T13:20:05.074Z","stars":22,"forks":3}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Lorgnette is a framework for augmenting code editors with malleable code projections, i.e., alternative representations that are bidirectionally linked to pieces of code (or even runtime data!) and can be created and modified by the users of the code editor. Lorgnette is a research prototype, currently targeting code editors that run in webpages, such as the Monaco editor and CodeMirror.","You can try out some of Lorgnette's projections by visiting the online playground environment (link below). At the moment, projections cannot be modified from within the playground itself. If you'd like to modify existing projections or specify your own, please clone the repository, modify the code according to the instructions below, and run your own build locally!","Try Lorgnette's playground in your browser! 🎮"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/exsitu-projects/lorgnette/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"a1cb44f0524ff268f1a694d6f6991341709bccdebb43adf6aaa9c0f4c15a4fa1","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T13:20:05.212Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T13:20:05.212Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Lorgnette is a framework for augmenting code editors with malleable code project